NAME
    spinner(1) - a playback program for HoverWare animations

SYNOPSIS
    spinner [-time] [-opt n] [-wire] [-rgb] [-windowid id] [-full] file

DESCRIPTION
    The spinner program will play back HoverWare animations to a
    resizable window.  The options to spinner are as follows:

	-time	Provide a frames-per-second rate on the console
		from which spinner was invoked

	-opt n	Override the default optimization level of all of
		the HoverWare objects in the animation.

	-wire	Play the animation in wireframe mode

	-rgb	Play the animation in color-per-vertex mode instead of
		texture mapped mode (which is the default)

	-windowid id	Given a specified window ID, spinner will play
		the animation in that window.  The window should be
		suitable for 3D graphics; that is, a truecolor, double-
		bufferable window, in the image planes, if possible

	-full	Play the animation in full-screen mode

    The window that the animation is playing in may be resized at any time;
    additionally, the following keyboard inputs are recognized:

	<space>	Toggle the pause state of spinner

	<r>	Restart the animation

	<q>	Exit spinner

    Spinner may also be exited by using the close menu item in the window
    menu.

SEE ALSO
    hw(3), gfx2hw(1)
